Z||000032||Dave Gunsul||10-13-2001||01:36 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR>[B]Oh yeah, he took home the "Chuck Warber" award at the show!<P>Don't mean to pick on you Minngreen but it's<BR>called the "Rich Warber" award. The best of show award was named that to honor a very good NIFE member that passed away.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Besides being a drag racer for most of his life Rich was the owner of the purple chop top V8 that everyone would love to own.<BR>Again, no flames meant but I thought I should<BR>set the record straight as Rich was a real nice guy and is still missed by all who new him.<P><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000033||Nashco||10-13-2001||03:49 AM||||I've seen pics of this car here and there on the forum.  I really <B>really</B> like it!  I have a goal of making my car look pretty similar.  I love the one piece side units, the spoiler, and the chin spoiler.  I plan on using a stock spoiler with large stantions, and glassing the chin piece to look like one, but basically the same thing.  I also want mine just a smidge lower, so the wheels are right at the fender lip.  The V8 would be sweet, but I'm more of a turbo guy myself.  Thanks for the pics, this car is a beauty.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||10
