Z||000037||DKOV||10-13-2001||11:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>... We did the engine work which is a new ZZ4 355 HP Chevy crate engine with TPI.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-229s.jpg">   <P>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Is that a Rear Strut Brace I see there in the bottom of the frame?  IF so, was it custom for this application or can a guy buy one?<P>West Coast sells one, but even though they SAY it will fit any year Fiero WITH a 3.4L engine conversion, when I called them to order it, they said NO... It won't fit.<P>What to do... what to do.<P>DKOV -<P>||||reg||1
Z||000038||MinnGreenGT||10-13-2001||02:10 PM||||DKOV-<BR>Contact Darrell Morse in Minnesota... he makes & sells them direct (check under the link at the top of the page to "Fiero Parts Vendors" and scroll down until you get to Darrell Morse in Elk River).  This is his work:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strut1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strut2.jpg"> <P>Darrell also does ported ThrottleBodies & Intakes for the V6 as well as custom parts when necessary.  He's a real personable guy and great to deal with, so give him a call!||||reg||1
