Z||000053||artherd||10-15-2001||03:18 PM||||Hi Lisa, indeed we'll see!  Will and I are trying to be the first to bust a getrag!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Most of us trying to do the 5-speed Northstars are junking the Cadilac ECM entirely, and going to a fully aftermarket computer (http://www.chrfab.com look under "ignitions")<P>Though some are trying to severely modify the Caddy ECM too.<P>The engine gets 27 highway MPG in a 5,000lb caddy...<P>Might even be good for around 30 in a stickshift fiero, but I'll never drive it like that, I PROMISE!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I want a Pacer limo with Aerosmith inside.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>GTMike: There's a lot of controversy about Northstars and 5 speeds. Most of the Northstar Fieros now have the Caddy auto tranny but it weighs an extra 500 lbs over the getrag. I know some people are workin on the Northstar/5 speed and only time will tell whether it will be reliable enough...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000054||mrfixit58||10-15-2001||05:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>GTMike: There's a lot of controversy about Northstars and 5 speeds. Most of the Northstar Fieros now have the Caddy auto tranny but it weighs an extra 500 lbs over the getrag. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hummm... I'm certainly no expert but I can't imagine that the difference between the Getrag and the Caddy auto is anywhere close to 500 lbs. A turbo-hydromatic 400 is a brute but is under 100 lbs. A transverse version is heaver still because of the integrated differential but still well under 200 lbs. Can anyone confirm the ACTUAL weight of the Caddy auto tranny?<P>Please note this is NO WAY intended as a slam or flame, I would just like clarification.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000055||72vinman||10-15-2001||11:27 PM||||Welcome to the forum Kaz.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> You have a very nice car there. I am sure you will get quite a bit of info off the forum. Have fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000056||Archie||10-15-2001||11:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Kaz:<BR><B>Hi there.<P>I am new to the forum.<BR>Glad to see my car on the web.<BR>Thank you<P>Kaz Okayama<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Kaz, Welcome.<P>I've had a couple people ask me what Brand and model are your wheels. I know they were imported, but can't remember the details. <P>Can you tell us here?<P>Archie<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-206s_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
